DTSTAMP:20260725T064035Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-40909411691045-48358543413288@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Created on-site at Stanford by artists from Papua New Guinea\,
  the garden contains wood and stone carvings of people\, animals\, and mag
 ical beings that illustrate clan stories and creation myths. Meet on the c
 orner of Santa Teresa and Lomita Drive.\n\nPublic Tours: Fourth Sunday of 
 each month at 11:30am\, rain or shine. \n\nAdmission Info\n\nTours do not 
 require a reservation and are free of charge.\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: h
 ttps://museum.stanford.edu/visit/tours-and-group-visits\nLast synced: 2026
 -07-24 23:40 PDT
LOCATION:Meet at the Papua New Guinea Sculpture Garden\, at the corner of 
 Santa Teresa & Lomita Drive.
URL:https://museum.stanford.edu/visit/tours-and-group-visits
END:VEVENT
